# The leading slash matters: in git `dir/` means "a directory with this name at
# ANY depth", `/dir/` means "only at the repository root". The broad form is
# written only where breadth is a decision.

# ── OS and editor junk ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# ── the state of a particular project, not of the studio ─────────────────────
# The project profile (stack commands, zones, the orchestrator's project id),
# the limit-usage ledger and everything the studio's instruments write live in
# `.studio/` NEXT TO the studio, not inside it. The rule is here in case the
# profile gets copied inside.
/.studio/
/project.conf
/zones.conf

# ── instrument snapshots ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `snapshots/` is the working output of health-check and usage-snapshot: it is
# recreated by a command, there are no reference files, it has nothing to do
# with history.
/snapshots/*
!/snapshots/.gitkeep

# ── local ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.local
*.log
/tmp/
